title: Nationalised Industries
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/cards/leyland.jpg
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and industry_timer <= 0
on-arrival: industry_timer = 4; month_actions += 1

= Nationalised Industries

[+ industry_secretary +] reports on the state sector. British Steel loses money every week, British Leyland is kept alive by subsidy, and the coal industry is a law unto itself. [? if privatisations > 0 : So far we have sold off [+ privatisations +] state enterprises. ?]

- @bail_out: Bail out British Leyland and British Steel.
- @cut_subsidies: Cut the subsidies and let them shrink.
- @privatise: Sell a state enterprise.
- @telecoms: Introduce a bill to sell British Telecom.
- @coal_stocks: Quietly build up coal stocks at the power stations.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@bail_out
subtitle: -2 budget. Saves jobs for now.
on-arrival: budget -= 2; industry_subsidy += 1; unemployment -= 0.5; c2_con += 1*(1-dissent); wet_dissent -= 4; dry_dissent += 6; economic_liberalism -= 2

The money is found, again. Sir Michael Edwardes keeps BL going on condition that he can close plants and face down the shop stewards.

@cut_subsidies
subtitle: +2 budget. Closures and redundancies. Requires a dry Industry Secretary.
choose-if: industry_dry = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [+ industry_secretary +] won't let the lame ducks die.
on-arrival: budget += 2; unemployment += 0.7; strike_wave += 1; union_power -= 3; c2_con -= 2; de_con -= 1; dry_dissent -= 4; wet_dissent += 4

Steelworks at Consett and Corby close, along with car plants and shipyards. Whole towns lose their main employer.

@privatise
view-if: asset_sales < 4
subtitle: +2 budget.
choose-if: policy_privatisation = 1 or industry_dry = 1 or economic_liberalism >= 50
unavailable-subtitle: Neither the party nor the public is ready for denationalisation.
on-arrival: asset_sales += 1; privatisations += 1; budget += 2; economic_liberalism += 2; ab_con += 1*(1-dissent); c1_con += 1*(1-dissent) if privatisations >= 3; dry_dissent -= 3; wet_dissent += 2

[? if asset_sales = 1 : The government sells its shares in British Aerospace. ?][? if asset_sales = 2 : Cable & Wireless goes to the market. ?][? if asset_sales = 3 : Britoil, the state's North Sea oil company, is floated. Ordinary investors queue for shares. ?][? if asset_sales = 4 : Associated British Ports is sold. ?]

@telecoms
view-if: bill_telecoms = 0 and telecoms_sold = 0 and asset_sales >= 2 and time >= bill_telecoms_wait
subtitle: +3 budget, and the biggest share issue in history, once it becomes law in about seven months.
choose-if: (policy_privatisation = 1 or industry_dry = 1 or economic_liberalism >= 50) and bill_room = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if bill_room = 0 : [+ bill_room_text +] ?][? if bill_room = 1 : Neither the party nor the public is ready to sell British Telecom. ?]
on-arrival: dry_dissent -= 2; wet_dissent += 2; bill_new = "telecoms"
call: bill_introduce

[+ industry_secretary +] publishes the Telecommunications Bill. British Telecom will lose its monopoly and then its owner: more than half of the shares are to be sold. The engineers' union announces a campaign of industrial action.

@coal_stocks
view-if: coal_stocks < 3
subtitle: -1 budget. Prepares for a future miners' strike.
on-arrival: coal_stocks += 1; budget -= 1

The Central Electricity Generating Board is told to build up coal stocks at the power stations and to convert some to burn oil. Nobody says why, and nobody needs to.
